# Optional GitHub token for registry reads (raises the API rate limit).
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Trusted server-to-server access to screenshot metadata. Do not prefix the
# secret with NEXT_PUBLIC_; it must never be included in browser bundles.
SCREENSHOT_WORKER_URL=https://screenshots-api.is-pinoy.dev
SCREENSHOT_WORKER_SECRET=

# Origin serving the og Worker's routes. The landing page asks it which
# portfolios have a stored capture — the same question its preview endpoint
# answers per card — so the section shows exactly the sites it has a picture of.
# Defaults to https://is-pinoy.dev; override to point a preview deploy at
# production, and leave unset locally, where the section falls back to showing
# the newest entries rather than reporting an unreachable Worker as "no
# previews yet".
OG_WORKER_ORIGIN=https://is-pinoy.dev

# Feature flags (lib/flags.ts + lib/flags-server.ts). Server-side only — none of
# this is ever sent to the browser. The keys match apps/dashboard's registry, so
# a flag switched on there is the same switch out here.
#
# Vercel Flags SDK key (`vf_server_...`). Every targeting rule lives in the
# Vercel dashboard, not in this repo.
#
# NOT needed on Vercel. Deployments carry VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN, and the client
# authenticates with it, taking the project from the token's project_id claim.
# Set this only where OIDC is unavailable: outside Vercel, or locally if you are
# not using `vercel dev`.
#
# Deliberately left commented out rather than blank. @vercel/flags-core only
# validates the key when it is *defined*, so an empty FLAGS= throws
# "Missing sdkKey" and every flag reads false, while an absent one falls through
# to OIDC. Blank is worse than missing — uncomment only to set a real value.
#
# Prefer pulling it over pasting it, and never commit it:
#   pnpm dlx vercel env pull .env.local
# FLAGS=

# Signs requests from the Vercel Toolbar to /.well-known/vercel/flags, which
# lets you list the flags and override them for your own browser. Optional —
# without it that endpoint refuses requests and flags still resolve normally.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
FLAGS_SECRET=
